// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 and GPIO2 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard
// pushbuttons Button A (P5) and Button B (P11); official mPython hardware
// docs (mpython.readthedocs.io board/hardware.html) map P5->GPIO0 and
// P11->GPIO2 (matching pins_arduino.h BTN_A=0, BTN_B=2), and list P5/P11
// as connected to "button A"/"button B".
// pfodWeb NOTE: onboard 3x WS2812 NeoPixel RGB LED strip confirmed on P7
// (= GPIO17, per mpython.readthedocs.io board/hardware.html "P7: Connected
// to RGB LED", corroborated by the official neopixel library example
// `Pin(17, Pin.OUT)` for the onboard RGB). GPIO17 is NOT present in this
// chip's chipGpios (excluded chip-wide as PSRAM-reserved, GPIOs 16-17) so
// it is deliberately left untagged - re-adding it would reverse a
// pre-existing chip-level exclusion, out of scope for this task.
